            <ArticleTitle>[Fracture of the sacrum caused by bone insufficiency in a pregnant woman].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>511-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sacral insufficiency fractures are not rare. They are well known in female patients over age 50 with osteopenia. One case occurring in a young pregnant woman is described. We did not find another case in the literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
